cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CARAS — Classification Accuracy and Regression Assessment Suite
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it and also cite Olofsson et al. (2014),
  whose estimators, variance formulas and area adjustment CARAS implements.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Örücü
    given-names: Ömer Kamil
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2162-7553
    email: omerorucu@sdu.edu.tr
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Landscape Architecture, Faculty of Architecture,
      Süleyman Demirel University, Isparta, Türkiye
repository-code: https://github.com/omerorucu/caras
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 2.0.0
abstract: >-
  CARAS is a QGIS plugin for design-based accuracy assessment, bias-adjusted
  area estimation and continuous-map agreement analysis between two rasters.
  It implements probability sampling designs (simple random, systematic with a
  random start, stratified random with proportional, Neyman, equal or
  rare-class-floor allocation), the stratified estimator and variance formulas
  of Olofsson et al. (2014), confidence intervals for overall, user's and
  producer's accuracy, F1 and class areas, bias-adjusted area estimation, and
  the quantity / allocation / exchange / shift disagreement decomposition of
  Pontius and colleagues. For continuous maps it reports RMSE with its
  systematic and unsystematic components, MAE, bias, the coefficient of
  determination reported separately from squared Pearson r, Willmott's indices,
  Lin's concordance correlation and seeded bootstrap confidence intervals. All
  runs are reproducible from a recorded seed, and every report carries the
  complete analysis provenance.
keywords:
  - QGIS plugin
  - accuracy assessment
  - error matrix
  - design-based inference
  - stratified sampling
  - area estimation
  - land cover
  - remote sensing
  - quantity disagreement
  - allocation disagreement
  - map validation
